<article class="publication-article privacy-page">
  <h1>Privacy</h1>
  <p class="lede">Here News measures how the site is used so we can report better and keep it free. We don't sell personal information.</p>

  <h2>What we measure</h2>
  <p>We use <strong>Google Analytics</strong> (through Google Tag Manager) to count visits and see, in aggregate:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>which stories are read, and how far people read them;</li>
    <li>how readers find us (for example from a search engine, social media or another website) and roughly where they are (city or region);</li>
    <li>which links people follow from our pages to other websites, including businesses we write about and our advertisers;</li>
    <li>how often ads are seen and clicked;</li>
    <li>what people search for on the site.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>Google Analytics uses cookies to tell visits apart. Google's own policy explains how it handles this data: <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites" target="_blank" rel="noopener">How Google uses information from sites that use its services</a>.</p>

  <h2>Links to other websites</h2>
  <p>When you follow a link from Here News to another website, the link may include a short label (such as <code>utm_source=herenews.net</code>) so that business can see the visit came from Here News. It doesn't identify you.</p>

  <h2>Local stories</h2>
  <p>To show stories from your area first, your browser may look up your approximate city from your internet address, using the service <a href="https://www.geojs.io/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">GeoJS</a>. This lookup is skipped if your browser sends a “Do Not Track” or “Global Privacy Control” signal. Your area choice is kept only in your own browser, and you can change it with the “Local stories” menu.</p>

  <h2>Advertising</h2>
  <p>Ads on Here News come directly from local businesses. They are chosen to match the story you're reading, not your personal browsing history.</p>

  <h2>Your choices</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>You can block or delete cookies in your browser settings, or use Google's <a href="https://tools.google.com/dlpage/gaoptout" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Analytics opt-out add-on</a>.</li>
    <li>Turning on “Do Not Track” or “Global Privacy Control” in your browser stops the location lookup.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>Questions? Email <a href="mailto:thehonanews@gmail.com">thehonanews@gmail.com</a>.</p>
  <p class="small">Last updated: November 2026.</p>
</article>
